1
00:00:19,693 --> 00:00:25,655
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the Sutta, Girimananda Sutta again, and one of the perceptions that need to be developed.

2
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:30,196
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the perception of dispassion?

3
00:00:31,556 --> 00:00:41,619
[SPEAKER_00]: And there's also the perception of cessation, but it's said in the same way, it's described the same way, dispassion and cessation.

4
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,940
[SPEAKER_00]: Here Bhikkhu, having gone into

5
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:02,095
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no craving, dispassion, nibbāna.

6
00:01:07,599 --> 00:01:17,427
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this type of perception can only start being developed after many others have been developed to it.

7
00:01:17,507 --> 00:01:20,910
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not something that you can... it's also... it seems like more of a result.

8
