[SPEAKER_01]: You can't be acting passionately, thinking about dispassion.

16
00:02:19,115 --> 00:02:27,621
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I'll just read another sutta which seems to relate in the Middle Length Discourse number 14.

17
00:02:29,222 --> 00:02:31,264
[SPEAKER_00]: A person named Mahanāma.

18
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:33,125
[SPEAKER_00]: He's speaking to the Buddha.

19
00:02:33,165 --> 00:02:37,448
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, For a long time, sir, I have understood your teaching like this.

20
00:02:37,828 --> 00:02:40,590
[SPEAKER_00]: Greed, hatred and delusion are corruptions of mind.

21
00:02:41,531 --> 00:02:46,935
[SPEAKER_00]: Despite understanding that sometimes my mind is occupied by thoughts of greed, hate and delusion,

22
00:02:47,828 --> 00:02:50,949
[SPEAKER_00]: I wonder what qualities remain in me that I have such thoughts.

23
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:57,772
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha replies, there is a quality that remains in you that makes you have such thoughts.

24
00:02:58,653 --> 00:03:04,135
[SPEAKER_00]: For if you had given up that quality, you would not still be living at home and enjoying sensual pleasures.

25
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:09,878
[SPEAKER_00]: But because you haven't given up that quality, you are still living at home and enjoying sensual pleasures.

26
00:03:11,818 --> 00:03:15,300
[SPEAKER_00]: Sensual pleasures give little gratification and much suffering and stress.

27
00:03:16,793 --> 00:03:24,177
[SPEAKER_00]: But when they do achieve their joy and pleasure, or something more peaceful than that, they will not return to sensual pleasures.

28
00:03:46,022 --> 00:03:52,204
[SPEAKER_00]: So long as they do not achieve the joy and pleasure that are apart from sensual pleasures and unbeneficial qualities.

29
00:03:52,304 --> 00:03:52,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

30
00:03:52,564 --> 00:04:02,007
[SPEAKER_01]: So, first thing to mention there is, people can sort of conclude on the basis of that paragraph that, aha!

31
00:04:02,187 --> 00:04:05,127
[SPEAKER_01]: So, here I am, attracted to sensuality.

32
00:04:05,948 --> 00:04:09,169
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me now find pleasure different to sensuality.

33
00:04:09,609 --> 00:04:11,969
[SPEAKER_01]: They will take my mind away from sensuality.

34
00:04:12,089 --> 00:04:14,510
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let me experience the jhāna,

35
00:04:15,507 --> 00:04:27,793
[SPEAKER_01]: If you read other suttas, though, the Buddha says that the only way to experience jhāna pleasure is to completely abandon sensual pleasure beforehand.

36
00:04:28,514 --> 00:04:43,021
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, I can't remember, I think in Siddhan Gautama Rinpoche, he said that one can experience jhāna, that develop jhāna, that abide in the first jhāna, without having thoroughly understood the gratification, danger, and the escape from sensuality, that's impossible.

37
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:55,366
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's impossible to have jhāna, to develop jhāna, to abide in jhāna, to cultivate jhāna, unless you have fully seen, developed the danger of sensuality, that perception, and fully lost interest in it.

38
00:04:57,267 --> 00:05:10,113
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you develop the jhāna, and if that's done sufficiently enough, let's say like that, the mind will lose even any underlying inclination to return to sensuality, if it becomes careless and falls off from jhāna.

39
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:16,423
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that quality needs to be developed, but the only way to develop it, that's like almost like a catch-22.

40
00:05:16,783 --> 00:05:19,725
[SPEAKER_01]: The only way to develop it is to first see the danger in sensuality.

41
00:05:19,765 --> 00:05:21,085
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already how you develop it.

42
00:05:21,506 --> 00:05:27,289
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the quality that Mahānāma needs to see, really, most acutely, is the danger in sensuality.

43
00:05:27,469 --> 00:05:36,775
[SPEAKER_01]: That will then result in the quality of pleasure different to sensuality, that then he can cultivate and not return to sensual pleasures.

44
00:05:36,855 --> 00:05:40,677
[SPEAKER_00]: There are abandoning sensual pleasures, withdrawing from them,

45
00:05:41,715 --> 00:05:46,559
[SPEAKER_00]: And over time, you don't automatically get jhāna.

46
00:05:46,619 --> 00:05:46,719
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

47
00:05:46,739 --> 00:05:49,141
[SPEAKER_00]: But you do feel joy.

48
00:05:49,481 --> 00:05:51,503
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yes, because you're free from danger.

49
00:05:52,424 --> 00:05:54,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the danger of sensuality does not apply to you.

50
00:05:54,726 --> 00:05:55,426
[SPEAKER_01]: You get the joy.

51
00:05:55,446 --> 00:05:59,910
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, you would get the joy if you just escaped a death trap or something.

52
00:06:00,911 --> 00:06:05,694
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might not have some other pleasure now, but you certainly have pleasure of freedom from a death trap.

53
00:06:06,695 --> 00:06:08,377
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's not a small thing.

54
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,078
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I'm saying.

55
00:06:10,158 --> 00:06:11,259
[SPEAKER_01]: It's important to recognize that

56
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:14,579
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't replace sensuality.

57
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:21,663
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't knock it out as a peg with another pleasure that's not sensual, because that principle is always sensual.

58
00:06:22,744 --> 00:06:30,068
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if people try to get the jhānas, and hoping that that will free them from sensuality, that will be the sensual meditation.

59
