00:07:23,442 --> 00:07:26,984
[SPEAKER_01]: His intention would want to be everywhere else but there.

66
00:07:27,804 --> 00:07:31,026
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the intention that must be cultivated towards sensual pleasures.

67
00:07:32,747 --> 00:07:34,208
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's sufficiently developed

68
00:07:34,782 --> 00:07:37,884
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already a form of, you know, a substantial freedom.

69
00:07:38,944 --> 00:07:48,169
[SPEAKER_01]: That then, if you dwell secluded like that for a while, that's then the pleasure of seclusion, that's developed beforehand, that then is accompanied later on by jhāna.

70
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:59,555
[SPEAKER_00]: Right, but so that's... that pleasure of withdrawal, that pleasure of seclusion, is a pleasure which, you know, which one can experience and... Yeah.

71
00:07:59,895 --> 00:08:00,976
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a pleasure of relief.

72
00:08:01,396 --> 00:08:02,357
[SPEAKER_01]: Relief from the danger.

73
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,260
[SPEAKER_01]: Not necessarily a jhāna.

74
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:08,121
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, but it's basically, it's prerequisite.

75
00:08:08,141 --> 00:08:08,702
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what he says.

76
00:08:08,782 --> 00:08:16,724
[SPEAKER_01]: Having been secluded from centrality, he experiences the pleasure on account of that seclusion from centrality, and then he enters and abides in jhāna.

77
00:08:17,324 --> 00:08:25,147
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the pleasure in jhāna is the pleasure of seclusion from centrality, not the pleasure of a mystical experience of jhānic absorption or something.

78
00:08:25,845 --> 00:08:45,530
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the pleasure of safety, the relief of safety, that then, if you dwell long enough, your mind will be established in correct thinking and pondering, there will not be spilling out into domain that doesn't pertain to you, the clarity will be established, the mindfulness will be unwavering, and that's the jhāna, on the basis of that pleasure of seeing the danger in sensuality and refusing to go there anymore.

79
00:08:47,750 --> 00:08:50,191
[SPEAKER_00]: So, any person

80
00:08:51,226 --> 00:08:55,827
[SPEAKER_00]: restrains their senses, sustaining that wild animal, and it calms down.

81
00:08:57,888 --> 00:09:05,550
[SPEAKER_00]: And there is a experience of calmness on account of that, which is peaceful, which is pleasant.

82
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:06,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

83
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:10,691
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's... that comes from not being wild, not letting this animal run wild.

84
00:09:10,731 --> 00:09:10,911
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

85
00:09:11,151 --> 00:09:13,552
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that pleasure is higher than sensual pleasure.

86
00:09:14,784 --> 00:09:15,384
